{"answer":"The critic's case concedes the very point that defeats it: the proposal explicitly tags suspended nodes as 'structurally refutable pending evidence'—an advisory, provisional classification of nodes in the undecided region—rather than committing them under the skeptical semantics. The flag operates exclusively on nodes the grounded extension has suspended, so it cannot override, contradict, or undermine any commitment the grounded extension actually makes, including root validity.\n\nThe demand that the two fixed points be proven unable to disagree on committed accept/refute sets is unnecessary because the proposal never treats co-grounded commitments as skeptical commitments. The co-grounded extension is used solely as a structural probe on the undecided region: it partitions suspended nodes by whether they are also excluded from the greatest fixed point. This is a diagnostic comparison performed entirely outside the skeptical semantics's committed sets; it imports no credulous verdict into the skeptical guarantee.\n\nA root committed under the grounded extension is, by definition, not in the undecided region and therefore never reaches the tagging mechanism. The flag cannot apply to it, so the scenario the critic constructs—a root committed under grounded semantics but refuted under the co-grounded extension—cannot arise through the proposed tagging. The guarantee that committed nodes are untouched is structural, not an unproved assumption: the mechanism is defined to act only on the grounded extension's suspended region.\n\nWhether the two fixed points can in principle disagree on their committed sets is immaterial to the proposal's validity. The proposal does not assert their agreement, rely on their agreement, or conflate their verdicts. It uses each fixed point for what it deterministically computes: the grounded extension for skeptical commitments, the co-grounded extension as a greatest-fixed-point boundary test on the remaining nodes. Since reinstatement is a derived property of each fixed point independently, and the flag never promotes a co-grounded verdict into a skeptical commitment, root validity is preserved by construction."}